ifdl (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Modernize packaging for current debhelper/dpkg-dev:
    - Switch to debhelper-compat (= 13) and a minimal dh(1) debian/rules
    - Bump Standards-Version to 4.6.2, mark package Architecture: all,
      add Rules-Requires-Root: no
    - Add debian/source/format (3.0 native)

  * Fix --force in both ifdl and ifset: the flag set its variable to "1"
    rather than "-f", so every copy ran as "cp 1 <file> <file>.bak" and
    failed. ifdl ignores copy failures, so -f silently brought the interface
    up on the previous location's configuration.
  * ifset: initialise $force alongside the other variables.

  * Modernise both scripts to current POSIX shell practice; shellcheck -s sh
    is now clean:
    - Replace the `for arg in $*` parsers with `while`/`case` loops, so
      arguments containing whitespace and location or interface names
      containing a dash (br-lan, coffee-shop) now work
    - $(...) instead of backticks, quote expansions, use [ p ] || [ q ]
      instead of the non-portable [ p -o q ]
    - Derive --list from a glob rather than parsing ls output

 -- Douglas Leonard <dleonard@dleonard.net>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 08:40:00 -0700

